agreement entered","kind":"deal","tone":"good"},{"label":"Material agreement terminated","kind":"deal","tone":"warn"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000114036126019761/0001140361-26-019761-index.htm"},{"date":"2026-05-07","form":"8-K","codes":["2.02","8.01"],"events":[{"label":"Results announced","kind":"results","tone":"blue"},{"label":"Other material event","kind":"news","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000174388126000018/0001743881-26-000018-index.htm"},{"date":"2026-03-30","form":"8-K","codes":["8.01","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Other material event","kind":"news","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000114036126011991/0001140361-26-011991-index.htm"},{"date":"2026-02-24","form":"8-K","codes":["2.02","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Results announced","kind":"results","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000174388126000008/0001743881-26-000008-index.htm"},{"date":"2026-02-12","form":"8-K","codes":["8.01","9.01"],"events":[{"label":"Other material event","kind":"news","tone":"blue"}],"url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000114036126004995/0001140361-26-004995-index.htm"}],"legal_events":[{"date":"2020-10-15","label":"Activist or control stake disclosed","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000119312520270273/0001193125-20-270273-index.htm","tone":"warn"},{"date":"2019-07-10","label":"Activist or control stake disclosed","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000114036119012746/0001140361-19-012746-index.htm","tone":"warn"},{"date":"2019-07-08","label":"Activist or control stake disclosed","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000090342319000277/0000903423-19-000277-index.htm","tone":"warn"},{"date":"2018-08-01","label":"Activist or control stake disclosed","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000119312518233959/0001193125-18-233959-index.htm","tone":"warn"}],"summary":{"sentences":["BridgeBio Pharma, Inc. files with the SEC under \"Pharmaceutical Preparations\", based in CA, and has been publicly reporting for 6 years.","It reported $542.4m of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 66.8% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 94.9%.","Listed on Nasdaq, it is still consuming cash, with roughly 14 months of runway at the current burn."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 66.8% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $194.5m in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000174388126000019/0001743881-26-000019-index.htm","accession":"0001743881-26-000019"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in 6 of the last 8 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000174388126000019/0001743881-26-000019-index.htm","accession":"0001743881-26-000019"},{"text":"Gross margin of 94.9% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001743881"},{"text":"Net cash of $884.2m against total assets of $1.4bn - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000174388126000019/0001743881-26-000019-index.htm","accession":"0001743881-26-000019"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 3812.0% across 8 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000174388126000019/0001743881-26-000019-index.htm","accession":"0001743881-26-000019"},{"text":"Gross margin compressed from 97.7% to 94.9% against the same quarter a year earlier. Either input costs are rising or the company is discounting to hold volume.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001743881"},{"text":"The company is loss-making at the operating line (-54.5% margin). Profitability is a forecast, not a fact.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000174388126000019/0001743881-26-000019-index.htm","accession":"0001743881-26-000019"},{"text":"The operating loss widened by $1.6m against the same quarter a year earlier - it is getting worse, not better.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000174388126000019/0001743881-26-000019-index.htm","accession":"0001743881-26-000019"},{"text":"About 14 months of cash at the current burn ($887.8m against $760.4m a year). A company that must raise is a company that raises on the buyer's terms.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000174388126000019/0001743881-26-000019-index.htm","accession":"0001743881-26-000019"},{"text":"Shareholders' equity is negative (-$2.3bn) - liabilities exceed assets on the balance sheet.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000174388126000019/0001743881-26-000019-index.htm","accession":"0001743881-26-000019"},{"text":"Insiders disposed of 14.4% of their combined holdings over the last four quarters (210,123 shares across 14 ownership filings). People with the best view of the business were reducing their stake.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000147083126000709/0001470831-26-000709-index.htm"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.6% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1743881/000147083126000709/0001470831-26-000709-index.htm"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 87.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"gross_margin","comparison":"below","threshold":0.87,"consecutive":2,"current":0.949,"current_display":"94.9%","threshold_display":"87.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Eight points of margin is a real deterioration rather than noise. Two consecutive quarters stops one bad quarter from forcing a sale.","editable":true},{"id":"growth_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Revenue growth falls below 33.0% for 2 consecutive quarters","metric":"revenue_growth_yoy","comparison":"below","threshold":0.33,"consecutive":2,"current":0.668,"current_display":"66.8%","threshold_display":"33.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"If growth halves and stays there, the reason you looked at this company has gone.","editable":true},{"id":"runway_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Cash runway falls below 12 months","metric":"runway_months","comparison":"below","threshold":12.0,"consecutive":1,"current":14.011,"current_display":"14 months","threshold_display":"12 months","fired":false,"rationale":"Below twelve months the company raises on whatever terms it can get, and that dilution lands on you.","editable":true},{"id":"dilution_ceiling","kind":"metric","label":"Diluted share count growth rises above 10.0%","metric":"dilution_yoy","comparison":"above","threshold":0.1,"consecutive":1,"current":0.024,"current_display":"2.4%","threshold_display":"10.0%","fired":false,"rationale":"Share count growth above this rate transfers your stake to new holders faster than the business is likely to compound.","editable":true},{"id":"going_concern","kind":"event","label":"Going-concern doubt appears in any filing","metric":"going_concern","comparison":"is_true","threshold":true,"current":false,"current_display":"not present","fired":false,"rationale":"The auditors saying the company may not survive the year is not a signal to interpret. It is the exit.","editable":false}],"team":[{"raw_name":"Charles J Homcy","role":"Director","title_filed":"Director","shares":919876.0,"sold_in_window":0.0,"bou